{
  "analysis": "All three classes miss small instances (low size-tertile recall 0.03/0.34/0.34; median missed 37-51px vs train median 73-90px). Inclusion is weakest (AP50 0.18, only 10 real images). Scratches have the highest FP rate (0.22/img). Round 1 tests three single-factor levers vs the balanced default control: (1) small scale range, (2) inclusion-heavy allocation, (3) cross-class background pool.",
  "candidates": [
    {
      "hypothesis": "Misses concentrate in the small size tertile for every class, so shrinking paste scale to 0.3-0.7 (covering the 25-60px missed range) should raise small-instance recall and mAP. Confirmed if inclusion AP50 jumps well above 0.18 and low-tertile recall improves vs control; if flat, scale is not the lever.",
      "allocation": {"inclusion": 17, "patches": 17, "scratches": 16},
      "params": {
        "inclusion": {"scale_min": 0.3, "scale_max": 0.7, "target_pool": "same_class", "source_weighting": "uniform", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": []},
        "patches": {"scale_min": 0.3, "scale_max": 0.7, "target_pool": "same_class", "source_weighting": "uniform", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": []},
        "scratches": {"scale_min": 0.3, "scale_max": 0.7, "target_pool": "same_class", "source_weighting": "uniform", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": []}
      }
    },
    {
      "hypothesis": "Inclusion's low AP50 (0.18) may be data scarcity (10 real images) rather than scale. Doubling its allocation (25/12/13) at the default scale should lift inclusion AP without hurting the other classes. Confirmed if inclusion AP50 rises more than in candidate 1/control while patches/scratches hold.",
      "allocation": {"inclusion": 25, "patches": 12, "scratches": 13},
      "params": {
        "inclusion": {"scale_min": 0.6, "scale_max": 1.4, "target_pool": "same_class", "source_weighting": "uniform", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": []},
        "patches": {"scale_min": 0.6, "scale_max": 1.4, "target_pool": "same_class", "source_weighting": "uniform", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": []},
        "scratches": {"scale_min": 0.6, "scale_max": 1.4, "target_pool": "same_class", "source_weighting": "uniform", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": []}
      }
    },
    {
      "hypothesis": "Scratches have the highest FP rate (0.22/img) and low-contrast instances are missed everywhere; pasting onto any_class backgrounds adds texture diversity and co-occurring defects, improving precision/robustness. Confirmed if precision (esp. scratches) improves vs control without recall loss.",
      "allocation": {"inclusion": 17, "patches": 17, "scratches": 16},
      "params": {
        "inclusion": {"scale_min": 0.6, "scale_max": 1.4, "target_pool": "any_class", "source_weighting": "uniform", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": []},
        "patches": {"scale_min": 0.6, "scale_max": 1.4, "target_pool": "any_class", "source_weighting": "uniform", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": []},
        "scratches": {"scale_min": 0.6, "scale_max": 1.4, "target_pool": "any_class", "source_weighting": "uniform", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": []}
      }
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Cand1 (small scale 0.3-0.7) confirmed the small-miss hypothesis: it gave the best mAP50 (0.604) and the best patches AP50 (0.79), with inclusion (0.355) and scratches (0.667) also strong. Cand2 (inclusion-heavy 25/12/13) was worse (0.584) — extra inclusion allocation did NOT beat balanced, so scarcity wasn't the main inclusion problem. Cand3 (any_class pool) badly hurt inclusion (0.208) while helping scratches precision, so cross-class backgrounds confuse inclusion. Control (default scale) was close (0.595) with marginally better inclusion/scratches but clearly worse patches (0.713). Cand1 has the highest mAP50 and beats control by 0.009 (>0.005), so the tiebreaker does not apply.",
  "choice": 1,
  "lesson": "Small paste scale (0.3-0.7) is the dominant lever: best mAP50 (0.604) and best patches AP50 (0.79), confirming the small-miss hypothesis. Balanced allocation beat inclusion-heavy, and any_class backgrounds badly hurt inclusion (0.21) — keep same_class + balanced + small scale. Next round: build on small scale and probe whether going even smaller (0.3-0.5) or prefer_small sources recovers the still-missed smallest instances, while keeping same_class pool."
}
